e] [17592186409815 1079 #uuid "ea7b226f-79df-5fde-bf3b-18e9fc4ba990" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409789 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409790 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409792 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409798 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409803 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1077 "selection" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409792 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409816 1079 #uuid "fe323417-1cf2-5a08-b6a1-9d36f7d769a5" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409817 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409814 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409817 1069 "q-35222" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409817 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409817 1071 "Find the vector $x$, if $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ and \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409817 1072 #uuid "4f44c2f3-4f54-5e93-a6f8-f1e6cfd5ee6a" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409817 1074 "We know that any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ has the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the coordinates relative to the basis $\\,B.$ Since we are told that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={{(\\,2\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{{(\\,5\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]= \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -25\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -21\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409818 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409813 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409818 1069 "q-112246" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409818 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409818 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409818 1072 #uuid "893314bd-9641-54d7-a9c3-9945a815ea4f" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409818 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 26\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 26\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-14 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=8.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(8)=-14\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=(-6)+8=2.$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409819 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409816 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409819 1069 "q-112211" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409819 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409819 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{2}?$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409819 1072 #uuid "d9b245f0-31aa-56fe-aa26-5663dd9e140f" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409819 1074 "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={{(\\,-8\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{1}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{1}}+{{(\\,-7\\,)}_{⏟}}_{{x}_{2}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{b}_{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nx=(-8)\\cdot {b}_{1}+(-7)\\cdot {b}_{2}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that ${x}_{2}=-7.$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409820 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409815 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409820 1069 "q-112251" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409820 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409820 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -38 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409820 1072 #uuid "ebceb075-efc9-5bc0-95d2-77852526cbc8" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409820 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -38 \\\\ 24\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives the system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{12}{19}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -19 & -38 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -19{x}_{2}=-38.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-5(2)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10+2=12.$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409821 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409812 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409821 1069 "q-76073" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409821 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409821 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409821 1072 #uuid "ec45397c-5ced-5a47-b9a9-86c6aa1d1bf3" 13194139533582 17592186045417 true] [17592186409821 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ \\,\\,-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ \\,\\,0=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the third equation is always false. Therefore, the system has no solution and we conclude that \n\n$$\nx\\notin \\text{Span}{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}.\n$$" 